    "body": "Document reference: OFFICIAL-SECONDARY-2024-04-10. Effective: 2024-04-10. Summary: This entry records the official astronomical classification of Pluto. The IAU classifies Pluto as a dwarf planet. This designation was established following criteria set by the International Astronomical Union. As a result, Pluto is not considered a major planet, but rather a distinct category of celestial body. Registry status: Active. The classification affects educational materials, scientific literature, and public understanding. This entry is authoritative for all institutional references. The value as written: yes. This record supersedes any previous classifications. All subsequent documentation must align with this determination. The Northline Institute maintains this registry for consistent reference."
